cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  research it accompanies. The preferred citation is the paper.
title: Kenning Encounter
type: software
abstract: >-
  An encounter-sequential substrate for an agent's own accumulated experience.
  Its temporal causality is integrated rather than borrowed: an internal chain
  of encounters, with authored coherence edges, auto-written provenance,
  bookmarked references to sources it does not copy, temporally ordered
  delivery, and a governed passive synthesis that puts held meaning in front of
  a decision. The firing layer that would make it anticipatory is deliberately
  withheld; see WITHHELD.md.
authors:
